.githooks/leak-deny.local
madb-cache/
openbd-cache/
# The fetch cache the passes write when they are run by hand. CI points `--cache` at the same name
# and never commits it either; a captured page belongs in data/fixtures/ where something states
# where it came from.
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Crash-recovery journal for data/names/*.yaml — facts learned since the last compaction. Exists
# only while a name pass is mid-flight and is replayed into the YAML on the next start, so it is
# transient state rather than data. The YAML beside it is the thing worth committing.
data/names/.journal/

# Local preview config; the server is a dev convenience, not project source.
.claude/

# Scratch directories an agent or a run leaves behind. Never part of the project.
.tmp-*/

# DERIVED, AND THE SITE REPOSITORY IS THE PUBLISHED SNAPSHOT. `deploy.sh` copies everything here
# except feed.json, titles.json and ledger.json, and all three are recomputed by build.py. One
# consequence worth knowing: titles.json is read by ADAPTERS, so a fresh clone must build once
# before it can fetch. The committed copy used to hide that ordering.
data/build/
# THE STORE IS DERIVED AND IS NOT COMMITTED, which `adapters/relational/__init__.py` states as the
# reason it is allowed to be load-bearing: deleting it costs one rebuild and nothing else. Listing
# it here does not untrack it, and it WAS tracked from before these lines existed, so four commits
# carry a 2.2 MB binary and one of them is from 2026-08-13. `git rm --cached` on that date is what
# made the rule true. `data/store.db` was the name before the rename and its file is deleted.
data/relational.db
data/relational-rebuilt.db

# Answers a check already worked out, keyed on the content they were measured from. Outside
# data/build on purpose: the green-tree token hashes that, and a cache written during a gate
# would invalidate the token the same gate is about to write. See adapters/filecache.py.
data/cache/
data/cache.set-aside/
